      "problem": "Find the disjoint union of the sets $\\{△,◻\\}$ and $\\{a,c,e\\}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the sets are disjoint since\n\n$$\n\\{△,◻\\}\\cap \\{a,c,e\\}=∅.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the disjoint union is simply the union:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{△,◻\\}⊔\\{a,c,e\\} & =\\{△,◻\\}\\cup \\{a,c,e\\} \\\\  & =\\{△,◻,a,c,e\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
